## Angular Frontend Conventions

- Project layout follows Angular CLI: sources in `frontend/src/` with modules, components, and services.
- Use RxJS and Observables for async data; avoid manual Promise chains when streams exist.
- Keep components presentational where possible; move data-fetching and business logic to services.
- Respect existing module boundaries and lazy-loading configuration in [frontend/angular.json](mdc:frontend/angular.json).
- Use translation helpers and existing i18n keys instead of hard-coded strings.
- Styles use SASS; prefer component-scoped styles and existing variables/mixins.
- HTTP calls should go through well-defined services; prefer interceptors for cross-cutting concerns.
- Testing: add `.spec.ts` alongside components/services.

Dev Workflow
- Run the Angular dev server with Rails proxy as configured in [frontend/cli_to_rails_proxy.js](mdc:frontend/cli_to_rails_proxy.js).
- Match TypeScript configuration in [frontend/tsconfig.json](mdc:frontend/tsconfig.json) and [frontend/tsconfig.base.json](mdc:frontend/tsconfig.base.json).
